<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:vc="clr-namespace:CoenQcCalibrateValve;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Delivers water on one valve at a reward's pulse width (Pip, 11 Nov 2026), so a valve's calibration can be checked by weighing what it gives: Pulses pulses of SizeMs on Channel at PulseGapMs, fired on the board's Harp clock as the calibration fires them (OpenRigs.Core FirePulses). rig-control's Calibrations page works out the width and the pulses from the valve's curve (1 ml at the reward size) and gives the curve's pulseGapMs; the board's port, its RewardValve lines and the lick spout stage come from this machine's rig.yml (ReadValveRig). On a rig with a lick spout stage the spouts go to the in position from PositionsFile first and out after (Extensions\Spouts.bonsai). Ready once the board answers and the spouts are in; Go fires the pulses, reporting each as the delivered metric; Finished once the last has closed. Nothing is written.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Settings</Name>
        <Description>RigConfigDirectory is &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;; ValveRig is what the delivery takes from rig.yml there (ReadValveRig, src\Extensions\ValveRig.cs): the board's port, its RewardValve lines and, on a rig with one, the lick spout stage's drivers.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:ResolveRigConfigDirectory">
                <orc:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</orc:ConfigRoot>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigDirectory</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ReadValveRig" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>ValveRig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Boolean">
              <rx:Name>SpoutsReady</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561, which the rig agent relays. Reports Recording at Go.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The behavior board on rig.yml's port (ValveRig), with the PulseController pulsing its RewardValve lines and no other: its TriggerCalibratedPulse fires one pulse of a given width on a line, as in a session. BehaviorBoard.Timestamps publishes the board's Harp clock as Timestamp. Ready 1 s after the board's first event, once the PulseController's setup has gone out, and once the spouts are in (SpoutsReady).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ValveRig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="PortName" Selector="PortName" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <PortName>UNMAPPED</PortName>
              <DumpRegisters>true</DumpRegisters>
              <Heartbeat>Enabled</Heartbeat>
              <EventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</EventsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ValveRig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="OutputPulseEnable" Selector="OutputPulseEnable" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.PulseController.bonsai">
              <BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>
              <OutputPulseEnable>DO1 DO2</OutputPulseEnable>
              <PulseDO1>10</PulseDO1>
              <PulseDO2>10</PulseDO2>
              <PulseDO3>10</PulseDO3>
              <BehaviorEventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BehaviorEventsSubjectName>
              <TriggerPulseSubjectName>TriggerPulse</TriggerPulseSubjectName>
              <TriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>TriggerCalibratedPulse</TriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.Timestamps.bonsai">
              <EventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</EventsSubjectName>
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Ready</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Channel" DisplayName="Channel" Description="The valve's behavior board line, 1 to 3 (DO1 to DO3): a RewardValve in rig.yml's wiring. rig-control gives it at launch." />
        <Property Name="SizeMs" DisplayName="SizeMs" Description="Each pulse's width in ms: the reward size's, read off the valve's curve by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="Pulses" DisplayName="Pulses" Description="How many pulses: 1 ml at the reward size, by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="PulseGapMs" DisplayName="PulseGapMs" Description="The off-to-on time between pulses, in ms: the valve calibration file's pulseGapMs, which rig-control gives at launch." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Deliver</Name>
        <Description>At Go, Pulses pulses of SizeMs on Channel at PulseGapMs through TriggerCalibratedPulse (DeliverTrain, src\Extensions, into OpenRigs.Core FirePulses on the Harp clock), each reported as the delivered metric (how many so far); once the last has closed, Finished, and Delivered ends, which takes the spouts out. Stops the workflow if Channel is not a RewardValve in rig.yml.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Channel" />
              <Property Name="SizeMs" />
              <Property Name="Pulses" />
              <Property Name="PulseGapMs" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ValveRig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DeliverTrain">
                <vc:Channel>1</vc:Channel>
                <vc:SizeMs>1</vc:SizeMs>
                <vc:Pulses>0</vc:Pulses>
                <vc:PulseGapMs>0</vc:PulseGapMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                <Property Name="WidthMs" Selector="WidthMs" />
                <Property Name="Count" Selector="Count" />
                <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                <orc:Line>1</orc:Line>
                <orc:WidthMs>1</orc:WidthMs>
                <orc:Count>0</orc:Count>
                <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ElementIndex" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Index + 1</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>delivered</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Last" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>Delivered</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="PositionsFile" DisplayName="PositionsFile" Description="On a rig with a lick spout stage, the positions file whose in position the spouts go to: rig-control gives the newest mouse's calibration\LickSpoutPositions\&lt;mouse&gt;.csv beside rig.yml; a path with no file there takes rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition. Required on a rig with a stage, unused on one without." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Extensions\Spouts.bonsai">
        <PositionsFile />
        <SpoutsForwardSteps>0</SpoutsForwardSteps>
        <DoneSubjectName>Delivered</DoneSubjectName>
        <DoneCommand>SpoutsOut</DoneCommand>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
